SPEC-TG-002: real Alembic migrations live in `migrations/` at the service root
(sibling to `src/`, i.e. `services/tool-integration-gateway/migrations/`), not
nested under this directory — `alembic.ini`'s `script_location` and every other
Python service in this monorepo (memory-knowledge-service, agent-runtime-service)
use that same top-level layout, which is also Alembic's own tooling convention
for a `src/` package layout. 13-package-and-class-design's own package tree
lists `adapters/db/migrations/` literally, but following that literally here
would fight Alembic's own `prepend_sys_path`/`script_location` conventions for
no benefit; this directory is kept only as the package-boundary placeholder
SPEC-TG-001 established, pointing to where the real thing actually lives.
